the paris commune a short-lived attempt  at revolutionary government that for  some holds a legendary place in history  famous for invoking images of french  workers taking up arms establishing  their own government and trying to  reforge france in a new image  its impact was and is far-reaching but  despite  said impact the commune only actually  existed for a little over two months  which raises the question  why why did the paris commune fail so  first  background in 1870 france was an empire  ruled by napoleon iii  there were some disagreements between  him and prussian leadership about who  would take the spanish throne someone  got offended and because this was 19th  century europe  that meant war the french did not  perform well in this war and napoleon  iii himself was even captured  and about six seconds after this  france's remaining leaders declared the  creation of the third french republic  but still continued the war  the prussian army now marched on paris  and placed the city under siege in  mid-september of 1870.  the city was mostly defended by the  national guard a voluntary militia made  up of the parisian  working class many of its members were  unhappy with the government and wished  for more representation and better  economic conditions for them if they  were expected to fight and die  they were given to use the technical  term squat and despite many protests and  increasing radicalization the  representatives of the french republic  remained in charge there and in january  1871 the city's leaders surrendered  the french held an election and the  pro-peace monarchists won  and as such many in paris feared the  return of the monarchy not napoleon iii  though  thrones are for winners with the war now  over the french government sought to  disarm all of those radical members of  the national guard  and so they came up with an ingenious  idea they asked politely and in return  promised not to shoot them shockingly  the national guard said no and when the  army moved in to seize their weapons  some fighting broke out many parisians  sided with the national guard and the  government and army fled the city  and on march the 18th the paris commune  was declared it held elections soon  after which were open to most parisians  providing they were men and a new ruling  council for the city was placed in  charge  most of these were radically left-wing  with many being socialists or communists  but about a quarter were moderate  right-wing candidates  however due to increasing radicalization  many of the right-wing members of the  council left and some even fled the city  in fact it was this diversity and  leadership which made running the  commune difficult  unlike later revolutions there was no  definitive leader nor much of a clear  agenda  however the primary debate of  legislators was over whether or not the  revolution was to be spread elsewhere or  shored up in paris first  in versailles not too far away the  freshly fled republican government was  deciding on how nice to be with the  revolutionaries  and the conclusion they came to was not  very the communards were little more to  the government than a violent coup led  by poor militiamen and such events could  never be allowed to slide if this  government was to survive  and in this opinion they have the  backing of most of the country the  commune had fairly broad support in  paris but nobody really knew what their  endgame was  and this is an important reason why it  would soon fail but how exactly did it  fail  well its end came when it was crushed  militarily the communists decided mostly  that sitting in paris was waiting to be  crushed and so decided in april to march  on versailles  they were clearly outgunned by the  french army but they banked on the  common soldier rejoining them as they  marched on versailles  now the military tacticians amongst you  will know that fighting a war based on  the premise of its fine they probably  won't shoot back  isn't the most sound strategy and it was  not as a side note whilst all of this  was going on there was a massive german  army camped outside the city  the reason that they were there was that  in the peace negotiations in return for  not storming the city the french would  give the germans to use a legal term fat  stacks of cash  and since the people of paris hadn't  paid up there they waited  anyway a couple of weeks after the  failed march on versailles the french  army launched an assault on paris  this assault is known as bloody weak  because it saw the french army  systematically eradicate most resistance  and undertake the mass execution of any  suspected communards  most communad leaders fled the country  and the government began the long  process of re-establishing control over  the city  and so like most small revolutions the  paris commune failed because it was  crushed militarily  and part of the reason why that could  happen was because of the fragmented  leadership of the commune there was no  central leader nor any overriding idea  of what the communades wanted france to  look like  and with that there was no decisive  action taken against the republican  government even when it was at its  weakest  nor was there any central ideology for  anyone outside of paris to rally around  and help them  i hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with a special  thanks to my patrons  james bissonette mr wolf kelly money  maker skye chappelle rob d martin  captain cydog marvin cassell moe aaron  the white adam stalter jordan longley  boogery wiggly gustav swan jerry landon  rasheed ali gareth turner maggie  patzkowski coppertone winston k wood  spinning three plates corso wolff  marcus asner spencer lightfoot matthew  shipley the mug whopper alex schwinn  lil brep and tc robert wetzel anthony  beckett charles the first and scottish  trekkie
 

